  "description": "Min Ji-Ho’s idol career as a member of a mid-tier K-pop group member ends in emotional turmoil and disappointment. Ready to leave the industry behind for good, Ji-Ho unexpectedly finds himself filling in on a variety show…only to cross paths with Kang Tae-Yeon, the A-list actor he’s long admired. A lighthearted moment on set quickly spirals into a headline-making scandal: the first same-sex “incident” in the industry. Though the rumors fade as quickly as they came, Ji-Ho’s quiet exit is once again delayed. When an awkward reunion with former groupmate Park Hyeon-Do pulls him back into old tensions, Ji-Ho is forced to confront not just his past, but the unresolved wounds he thought he left behind with his life as an idol. In a world where appearances are everything, can Jiho uncover what he truly wants…and who he wants to stand beside him when the cameras are off?\n\n(Source: Lezhin US)",
